        "question": {
          ":question/id": "bb80c161-44e6-5610-9f1c-fcdbbb4440dc",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and  $det(A)=-3?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is invertible\n\n- **II.** $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(A)=7$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=7=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-3\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
